  "worked_solution": "First, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }(4{x}^{13}) & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }(4\\cdot {x}^{13}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph $y={x}^{13}$ is power function with an odd positive power and therefore has the property that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{13}=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nMultiplication by the positive constant $4$ does not affect the limit at infinity. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{13}={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{x}^{13}=-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }(4{x}^{13})=-\\infty .\n$$",
